From 91724a90f2e9ac012b9e8f7ed025756594d91a6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clifford Swartz <cliffordswartz1@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:25:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/57] hw/char, hw/gpio, hw/arm: SERCOM USART and PORT models,
 LED0 and SW0

Peripheral Pretender v0, part B. mchp-sercom models the SERCOM USART
(one-character transmit buffer plus shift register, two-character
receive buffer, DRE/TXC/RXC per DS60001632H chapter 30) on a chardev,
with an optional "pace-tx" frame timer; SPI and I2C modes only store
their registers. mchp-port derives the pads from DIR/OUT/PINCFG/PMUX,
handles WRCONFIG and the IOBUS view, and exposes "port-out"/"port-in"
GPIO lines (-1 = not driven) plus per-group QOM properties.

The SoC uses both models in place of their generic register blocks.
The pic32cm-jh01-cpro board wires LED0 (PC05, active low) to a QEMU LED
and adds the machine property "sw0-pressed" for SW0 (PB19). New qtests
pic32cm-jh-sercom-test and pic32cm-jh-port-test; board docs updated.

Peripheral Pretender downstream patch; not for upstream submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
